name c01m02-the-last-sacrifice
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T17:08:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 2 OF 10 -- {The Last Sacrifice} [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: "eliminate all ground support in the quadrant" -- 12 T-80s and 5 fuel tanks. The
# 8 Werewolves in the air are NOT goals, which is the one thing this mission's verdict turns on.
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 1 (Alto Mayo, Peru, terrain.md 6), day -- sun +81.37 deg at the lead's
# spawn, computed by the runner. 17 starred objects, unlock marker none - open from the start.
# THE CAST: 8 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 12 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 5 fuel tank -> `target_soft` -
# wingman -> `f16`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 6, Stinger 10, artillery 5, wingman 6, fuel
# 20000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 100` = 20000 against
# the campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no
# mechanism; the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all 17 ground goals. The 8 Werewolves are NOT goals, so a run that killed
#   every Werewolf and no tank would be a FAIL -- and if a harness ever reports Werewolf kills here as
#   progress, the harness is wrong. In this tree the question cannot arise from the other side either:
#   nothing can kill a Werewolf (D2).
#   exit 3 = the expected reading; report the met count.
#   exit 1 on `lead` = the leader was shot: a mission loss. exit 1 on `two` alone is a damaged flight.
#   exit 2 = an engine finding (D1).

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): FOUR OF SEVENTEEN.
#   t = 40.3 / 44.1 s   two Mk-82 away, aimErrM 4.56 and 4.78; four T-80s die (t05+t06 and t03+t04,
#                       two stacked pairs)
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 4 of 17 met, `survive` met; `two` SUCCESS. No SAM in this
#                       mission at all -- it places no type-5 object -- so nothing shot at anybody.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m02 1
  spawn -6.05892 -76.98615 150 342.6 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp -6.01167 -77.00105 150 300
  wp -5.97735 -77.01188 1000 300
  objective kill unit f01
  objective kill unit f02
  objective kill unit f03
  objective kill unit f04
  objective kill unit f05
  objective kill unit t01
  objective kill unit t02
  objective kill unit t03
  objective kill unit t04
  objective kill unit t05
  objective kill unit t06
  objective kill unit t07
  objective kill unit t08
  objective kill unit t09
  objective kill unit t10
  objective kill unit t11
  objective kill unit t12
  objective survive

